  "scope": "# Conditional native qualification of lean NTP\n\nThe first unexecuted queue is retired with its exact source snapshot. Prelaunch\nreview caught argument abbreviation consuming the legacy replay checkpoint\nargument. Version two uses exact parsing and a regression covering both warm\nand replay forwarding, including rejection of a wrong resume checksum. Neither\nthe retired queue nor this replacement changes the main campaign's deadline or\nadvancement gate. No native phase ran in the retired queue.\n\nThis implements the gate fixed in the lean preparation before any new main\noutcomes. Wait without chips for the entire five-endpoint fixed-control study,\nincluding all independent scoring and gradient audits. Preserve its original\nclock. A stopped predecessor never authorizes this follow-up.\n\nProceed only when both training seeds favor recurrence against each work\ncontrol and both two-seed mean gains reach 0.01 nats. Recompute this from all\nsix frozen contrasts, without rounding or selecting a favorable control. A\nfailed development gate ends this queue with zero native work. It does not\nchange the predecessor's conclusions or spend confirmation alpha.\n\nIf eligible, admit only the prepared numerical qualification: deterministic\none/two fully differentiated passes, original qualification-only initializer,\nFP16 body, primitive FP32 attention, FP32 head/masters/moments, manual scale\n8192, and the existing changing 1e-4 qualification schedule/runtime optimizer.\nThe unused auxiliary head and loss are absent. The old worker selector\n`poisson2` receives the frozen all-(2,2) table; no depth sampling occurs.\n\nUse the existing 121-update warm and one-update fresh-process replay engines,\nwith explicit owned non-ephemeral communication ports. A thin outer wrapper\nvalidates the exact phase, source list, preparation, plan and resume checksum.\nIt leaves the already frozen constructor/preparation unchanged. Both warm\nprofiles run on separate eight-chip halves, with CPU checks overlapping replay.\nNo shared container cleanup and no change to the running scientific workers.\n\nRequire all-replica equality, initial local gradients, full 512-window trained\ngradients against pinned upstream CPU FP32, independent first optimizer steps,\nexact restored full state/RNG, and the existing 2% named update/moment replay\ngate. Compare replay gradients against the same independent CPU vector too.\nReport bit equality separately; this does not promise identical future paths.\nReject unexpected fallbacks, nonfinite values, missing phases or failed gates.\n\nFreeze a one-hour qualification clock only after admission. Bound each native\nphase to 900 seconds and CPU phase to 1,200 seconds. The complete estimate uses\nthe slower measured full-head 100-update rate with a 50% margin, four cold\nlaunches, two independent CPU audits and replay checks. Require at least 65 GiB\nfree on NVMe before admission, plus the protected 35 GiB filesystem, 512 GiB\navailable-memory and 10,000-inode reserves. Count 244 qualification updates,\nextra probes, CPU optimizer steps, all failures and setup/scoring tails. Saved\nsuccessful closures can be reused after controller recovery, while the\noriginal clock and exact saved source/path lists remain fixed. Partial phases\nrequire an explicit recovery registration, not an automatic rerun.\n\nThe queue's latest admission time is the predecessor's original deadline plus\n600 seconds. Waiting uses zero chips; do not add its elapsed time again to the\npredecessor's instance reservation. Qualification costs start at qualification\nadmission and remain separate from that waiting interval.\n\nStop after numerical/throughput qualification. This admits no LR search,\nscientific fit, adoption of qualification weights, held-out quality readout,\nTEST access, reserve access or terminal alpha. A lean scientific comparison\nwould need original random scientific weights, complete matched work and its\nown measured frozen budget. The research objective remains unachieved here.\n"
